<ul>
<li class=""><a href=#idempotency class="">Idempotency</a></li>
<li class=""><a href=#activity-parameters class="">Parameters</a></li>
<li class=""><a href=#activity-type class="">Activity Type</a></li>
</ul>
<p>An Activity Definition is a normal function or method that executes a single, well-defined action.
The same Activity Definition can be started as a <a class="" href=/workflow-activity>step in a Workflow</a> or as a background job using a <a class="" href=/standalone-activity>Standalone Activity</a> once it's been <a href=#worker-registration class="">registered with a Worker</a>.</p>
<p>An Activity Definition is the code that gives rise to an <a class="" href=/tasks#activity-task-execution>Activity Task Execution</a>.</p>
